'' sizeof( cva_list ), on every target. MEASURED from fbc, which emits the width as
'' the length of the memset at the declaration:
''
''     win64   __builtin_memset( &ARGS$1, 0, 8ll )
''     linux   __builtin_memset( &ARGS$1, 0, 24ll )
''
'' win32's was 4, the pointer width there, and it had a test of its own until the
'' 32-bit target was removed (D14).
''
'' NOT derivable from the pointer width. On Linux a va_list is the SysV register-save
'' record -- three words -- where on Windows it is one pointer. Reserving 8 bytes for
'' a 24-byte object is a stack overwrite that lowers and verifies cleanly, which is
'' why it is pinned here rather than left to the type table's own golden.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-types tests/lexer/src/basics.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: cva_list               size=  8 align= 8
